 "answer": "On a GPU with 32 GiB of VRAM, Ollama should default to a **32,768-token (32k) context length**. Recent Ollama versions pick the default from available VRAM, using these tiers as I understand them:\n\n- Less than 24 GiB: 4,096 tokens\n- 24 to 48 GiB: 32,768 tokens\n- 48 GiB or more: 262,144 tokens\n\nI'm not certain of the exact cutoffs in every release, so check the Ollama docs for your version. You can override the default with the `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH` environment variable or the `num_ctx` parameter in a request or Modelfile.",
